AND POOR DRAINAGE URBAN AREAS WILL BE POSSIBLE.<br>
WIDESPREAD THUNDERSTORMS WITH HEAVY RAINFALL ARE EXPECTED TONIGHT AS A
LOW PRESSURE SYSTEM. RAPID PONDING AND FLOODING OF POOR DRAINAGE AREAS
WILL BECOME COMMON THIS MORNING.<br>
ANY ADDITIONAL RUNOFF FROM THESE EXPECTED RAINFALL AMOUNTS COULD
AGGRAVATE THE FLOODING CONDITIONS.<br>
THE FLOOD WARNING CONTINUES FOR THE FOLLOWING RIVER. SEVERAL ROUNDS OF
SHOWERS AND THUNDERSTORMS TODAY AND TONIGHT HAVE THE POTENTIAL TO
PRODUCE 1 TO 2 INCHES OF RAINFALL ACROSS THE AREA. WILLMAR 411 AM CDT
FRI MAR 30 2007 . ADDITIONAL RAINFALL OF ONE TENTH TO ONE QUARTER INCH
CAN BE EXPECTED ACROSS MUCH OF EAST CENTRAL KANSAS AND WEST CENTRAL
MISSOURI THROUGH 5 AM. AND IN THE BLACK RIVER FALLS TO NEILLSVILLE
WISCONSIN AREAS.<br>
